From: Riven DS port
Subject: [PATCH] pack the tWAV Data-chunk header to its 20-byte on-disc size

Same class of bug as 0001, in the sound reader this time.

A tWAV Data chunk begins with a 20-byte big-endian header: uint16 sampleRate,
uint32 sampleCount, uint8 bitsPerSample, uint8 channels, uint16 encoding,
uint16 loop, uint32 loopStart, uint32 loopEnd. Declared without packing it
lays out as 24 bytes on every normal ABI -- two bytes of padding after
sampleRate to align sampleCount, and two more after loop to align loopStart.

vaht_wav.c:110 then does vaht_resource_read(res, sizeof(header), &header),
so every field after sampleRate is read from the wrong offset. `encoding`
lands on unrelated bytes, fails the tWAV_ADPCM test at vaht_wav.c:201, and
vaht_wav_open returns NULL with "Unsupported format..." for EVERY sound in
the game. data_seek is also left four bytes past the true start.

Upstream never sees this because its autotools build compiles everything with
-fpack-struct=1 (src/Makefile.am:8). Any consumer that builds the sources
directly -- as this project's CMake does, to stay cross-compilable to Windows
without autotools -- gets the padded layout instead.

#pragma pack rather than __attribute__((packed)), for the same reason as 0001:
the converter is built with MSVC on Windows.

diff --git a/src/vaht_wav.c b/src/vaht_wav.c
index ce96f2f..a42754b 100644
--- a/src/vaht_wav.c
+++ b/src/vaht_wav.c
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@ static inline void handle_data(vaht_wav* wav, uint32_t chunk_size)
     /* this chunk_size LIES, so fix it up */
     chunk_size -= 8;
     
+#pragma pack(push, 1)
     struct
     {
         uint16_t sample_rate;
@@ -106,7 +107,8 @@ static inline void handle_data(vaht_wav* wav, uint32_t chunk_size)
         uint32_t loop_start;
         uint32_t loop_end;
     } header;
-    
+#pragma pack(pop)
+
     vaht_resource_read(wav->res, sizeof(header), &header);
     VAHT_SWAP_U16(header.sample_rate);
     VAHT_SWAP_U32(header.sample_count);
